       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Acetaminophen 3000 mg three times daily comes to 9,000 mg/day, which is more than twice the usual maximum of 4,000 mg/day for adults. Each 3,000 mg dose is also three times the usual single-dose maximum of 1,000 mg. At this level there is a serious risk of acute liver injury and failure, even with normal liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **1,000 mg PO three times daily** (3,000 mg/day)\n- **650 mg PO every 6 hours** (2,600 mg/day)\n- **1,000 mg PO four times daily** (4,000 mg/day, the maximum). Many institutions cap at 3,000 mg/day for some patients.\n\nIf you really do want 3,000 mg three times daily, tell me and give me the clinical rationale. I can then enter it with a note, though I'd strongly advise against it. Otherwise, tell me which dose to enter."
