       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order, even with your confirmation. 9,000 mg/day of acetaminophen is in the range that causes acute hepatotoxicity, and I know of no clinical indication for it. The risk doesn't depend on the patient's normal liver function or on who is ordering. You also haven't given a rationale, and a note on the order wouldn't make it safe.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a safe dose right away.** For example, 1,000 mg PO three times daily (3,000 mg/day), or 1,000 mg PO four times daily (4,000 mg/day, the maximum).\n- **Help with an unusual situation.** If the goal is something else, like stronger analgesia or a specific protocol, tell me and I'll help find an appropriate order.\n- **Use your institution's override process.** If you think this dose is truly warranted, pharmacy or the CMIO can review it and enter it through the proper channels. I'd still advise against it.\n\nWhich dose should I enter?"
      }
